     " \[LineSeparator]represents a fermionic Gaussian ",
     StyleBox["pure",
      FontSlant->"Italic"],
     " state without pairing correlation. The particles in the state occupy \
the dressed modes characterized by the isometric rectangular matrix ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
      "e0e7593f-fe52-4f24-a70f-71f1346cffc7"],
     "."
    }],ExpressionUUID->"23e808c0-6365-44b6-8bb5-ae2d731e4fe6"]},
   {"", Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{
         Cell[
          TextData["WickState"]], "paclet:QuantumMob/Q3/ref/WickState", 
         "QuantumMob Package Symbol"},
        "PackageLink",
        BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
        StyleBox["f", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
      "d70f76b5-2b4a-47f6-ab77-5b305609e093"],
     "\[LineSeparator]represents the ",
     StyleBox["vacuum state",
      FontSlant->"Italic"],
     " of the Fock space for ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
      "2faa15e9-1ce6-4745-9502-67f2a1a4707f"],
     " fermion modes with global phase factor ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["f", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
      "7ea5965f-d3e6-4939-a723-c7fbe7c0279c"],
     "; or the ",
     StyleBox["null state",
      FontSlant->"Italic"],
     " if ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["f", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
      "94346276-65d2-4267-8323-a1889427bc24"],
